    "lawCode": "Amd §9, Chap 401 of 2002",
    "lawSection": "Nassau County",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7649\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend chapter 401 of the laws of 2002, amending the real\nproperty tax law and the Nassau county administrative code relating to\nassessment and review of assessments in the county of Nassau, in\nrelation to extending certain provisions thereof\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo extend provisions of Chapter 401 of 2002 until June 30, 2018.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection one amends subdivision 8 of section 9 of Chapter 401 of 2002\nto extend the provisions of such act set to expire on June 30, 2016,\nuntil June 30, 2018.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nChapter 401 of 2002 reformed the assessment review procedure in Nassau\nCounty. The amendments strengthened the Assessment Review Commission's\n(ARC) ability review and resolve challenges and gave the ARC\nsufficient time to review and resolve assessment grievances before the\nassessment roll becomes final. These provisions are currently set to\nexpire on June 30, 2016, this bill would extend the provisions for an\nadditional two years.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
